    {
      "vulnerability": {
        "@id": "https://ubuntu.com/security/notices/USN-9176-1",
        "name": "USN-9176-1",
        "description": "Stephan Lipp discovered that Ruby incorrectly handled converting the case of certain strings. An attacker could possibly use this issue to cause a denial of service or execute arbitrary code. (GHSA-34m4-m9fh-gqp5)  Owais Lone discovered that Ruby incorrectly handled compiling certain large regular expressions. An attacker could possibly use this issue to cause a denial of service or execute arbitrary code. (GHSA-3p8q-wmhx-vm2w)  Stephan Lipp discovered that Ruby incorrectly handled converting certain regular expressions to strings. An attacker could possibly use this issue to cause a denial of service or execute arbitrary code. (GHSA-7whj- cfh7-xgm4)  Stephan Lipp discovered that Ruby incorrectly handled memory when parsing certain regular expressions. An attacker could possibly use this issue to cause a denial of service or execute arbitrary code. (GHSA-7x2q-68qv-6p8x)  It was discovered that Ruby incorrectly handled converting the case of certain large strings. An attacker could possibly use this issue to cause a denial of service or execute arbitrary code. (GHSA-87fm-7w84-j2px)  It was discovered that Ruby incorrectly handled certain case-insensitive regular expressions. An attacker could possibly use this issue to cause a denial of service or obtain sensitive information. (GHSA-pvgc-g7gj-pv6h)  Stephan Lipp discovered that Ruby incorrectly handled certain case- insensitive regular expressions. An attacker could possibly use this issue to cause a denial of service or obtain sensitive information. (GHSA- wpqw-5qxg-m68r)",
        "aliases": []
      },
